<h2 class="alumni__heading" id="software">Software</h2>
<div class="page__inner">
  <div class="page__body">
    <p>We release the code behind our papers whenever we can. Code lives on our GitHub organisations: <a href="https://github.com/AIM-Imperial">AIM-Imperial</a> and, from our Houston years, <a href="https://github.com/UH-AIM">UH-AIM</a>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/UH-AIM/3D-Printing-Knits-release">3D-Printing-Knits-release</a> - design and analysis code for 3D-printed knitted fabrics, from our PNAS paper.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/UH-AIM/bistable-auxetic-surface-structures">bistable-auxetic-surface-structures</a> - cell library and inverse-design code for <a href="/projects/bistable-auxetic-surfaces/">bistable auxetic surface structures</a>, from our SIGGRAPH paper.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="alumni__heading" id="mechanics-applets">Mechanics applets</h2>
<div class="page__inner">
  <div class="page__body">
    <p>Single-file, browser-based simulations of the classic load cases of solid mechanics, built for teaching. Each applet runs directly in the browser, and each comes with a short derivation of the governing equations.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/sims/axial-stretching.html">Axial rod stretching</a> (<a href="/sims/derivations/axial-stretching.pdf">derivation, PDF</a>)</li>
      <li><a href="/sims/cantilever-bending.html">Cantilever beam bending</a> (<a href="/sims/derivations/cantilever-bending.pdf">derivation, PDF</a>)</li>
      <li><a href="/sims/torsion.html">Shaft torsion</a> (<a href="/sims/derivations/torsion.pdf">derivation, PDF</a>)</li>
      <li><a href="/sims/shear-beam.html">Shear beam</a> (<a href="/sims/derivations/shear-beam.pdf">derivation, PDF</a>)</li>
      <li><a href="/sims/buckling.html">Euler buckling</a> (<a href="/sims/derivations/buckling.pdf">derivation, PDF</a>)</li>
      <li><a href="/sims/plate-stretching.html">Uniaxial plate stretching</a> (<a href="/sims/derivations/plate-stretching.pdf">derivation, PDF</a>)</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
